From 7bee7b0a086bee6040c9630b65dd409977b65724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:30:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Player information] ALLM, QMS and FreeSync on one
 row, to make room for the connection and the sound

The column of the system page that says what the display declares is full: with the rows of the connection and
the sound formats it took 630 of its 564 px where every row shows its longest value (skin_check of
tools/regress/playerinfo). ALLM, QMS and FreeSync, three rows of a yes or a no, are one row now, "Also declares",
with those that the EDID declares (hades.tv.features, "none" without any; the three keys before it go). The sound
leaves AC-3 out, which every display with sound takes, so that the formats that tell a TV from a sound bar (DTS,
DTS-HD) fit on one line in font12; "Via sound bar/receiver (2.2.0.0)" too. The column takes 498 px again, as before
these rows.
---
